venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
agent/.cache/
models/*
!models/satquery_model.onnx
!models/class_config.json
outputs/
node_modules/

# data/ is ignored wholesale (the reBEN/benchmark/eval source data and all
# runtime-generated state are large and/or machine-local) EXCEPT the two
# real data sources the deployed app actually reads at startup -- see
# Dockerfile / api/scenes.py's ensure_scenes_loaded() and
# ensure_demo_change_scene_loaded(). A bare `data/` ignore (the line this
# replaced) blocks `!` negations for anything under it -- git can't
# re-include a path whose parent directory is itself excluded -- so this
# uses `data/*` instead, the same negation-friendly pattern already used
# for models/* above.
data/*
!data/demo_patches
!data/oscd
data/oscd/*
!data/oscd/test.parquet
# data/oscd/train.parquet (25.9 MB) is never read (OSCD_DEMO_SPLIT="test"
# in api/scenes.py) and data/oscd/_extracted/ is a runtime-regenerated PNG
# cache, not source data -- both stay ignored by the data/oscd/* line above.
